    "body": "## Changes requested\n\n1. The PR updates `main`, but the existing immutable `reusefirst/v1.2.0` tag\n   still contains `CANDIDATE_UNRELEASED` and `publication_approved: false`.\n   The PR therefore does not reconcile the release it claims to reconcile.\n   Either prepare a correctly versioned follow-up release or explicitly scope\n   this PR as metadata for a future release without marking v1.2.0 released.\n\n2. `PROVENANCE.md` asserts factory and product Customer Zero dogfood, but the\n   public repository contains no evidence or reviewable reference for that\n   claim. Add canonical, privacy-safe evidence or keep the claim out of the\n   public provenance.\n\n3. `RELEASE_NOTES.md` labels these changes `v1.2.0` even though that tag already\n   exists and is unchanged. Use a new version/release process, or label this as\n   unreleased main metadata.\n\nNo approval: the current patch leaves the canonical tag and the default branch\nwith contradictory release state.\n",
